# Styles

Use these styles to make a Home Assistant dashboard, a Civica card or a household guide clear and consistent. Choose a style by its job first, such as body text, a card edge or an error. Then take its value from the page that owns it.

The same styles apply to native Home Assistant screens, Civica custom cards and the examples in this guide.

## Colour

- [Colour](colour.html): choose the right palette for the job, see the theme colours a household can choose, and follow the rules for every colour.
- [Web-app colours](colour-web-app.html): the palette and functional colours for dashboards, web pages and the Companion app, ready to copy.
- [Print colours](colour-print.html): CMYK and Pantone values for printed guides, labels and signs.
- [Social colours](colour-social.html): colours and pairings for social media posts and release pictures.
- [Chart colours](chart-colour.html): one colour and pattern for each device or energy source in a chart.
- [Map colours](colour-maps.html): colours for base maps, zones and locations, with a working map.
- [Illustration colours](colour-illustrations.html): how to choose, pair and contrast colours in an illustration.

