## Use a role before a value

Choose a role, then use the Civica theme variable for it. For example, use the focus variable on a custom button instead of copying a yellow that looks close. The variable follows the household's theme colour and light or dark mode. A copied value does not.

The palette data lives in `design-system/palettes.json` in the repository. Themes and YAML are generated from it, so do not treat a value on a guide page as a second source.

## Know who owns what

- The style pages are guidance for a Home Assistant interface. They are not a brand for a household.
- For a family name, crest or business logo, follow [Personalise your home](../get-started/personalisation.html).
- The Civica [project identity](brand.html) is only for this guide and for promoting the project.
- The [design-system audit](../community/design-system-audit.html) lists the changes still to make to these pages.

